2. In these Rules —
“keep”, in relation to a cat or dog, means to keep the cat or dog permanently or temporarily for any duration of time;
“lessee” includes any licensee, tenant or owner of any property;
“property” means any property licensed, leased or sold or otherwise provided by the Board under the Act.

4. A lessee of any property must allow an officer of the Board or any person authorised by the Board to enter the property at any reasonable time to ascertain any of the following:
(a)whether any cat or dog is kept in the property;
(b)the number of cats kept in the property;
(c)the number and breed of dogs kept in the property.
